 "name": "x10",
 "description": "Direct-drive spring sprinter: no gears, no chains. The rear axle runs straight through the bores of two pullback\nmotors (every tooth mesh costs 28 % of the force in this drive; a spring motor also has no back-EMF sag and almost no\nrotor inertia), with one r31.3 wheel between them, sized so the spring's 600 rpm is a useful 2 m/s.\nThe front axle guides: r12 train wheels on the 8 mm plank between r15.2 tyres hanging 3.2 mm beside it.\nAAA battery stands low, crosswise between the axles on a 4x10 plate under the walls. No program, no stop.",
